Direct3D 9: the files of the Direct3D 9 part into the driver, and its entry point exported

The Direct3D 9 part (windows/mesa/overlay-virgl, D3D9*) is built into the same DLL as the
Direct3D 10 driver, as in the Yttrium project's Mesa fork it comes from, and the DLL exports
OpenAdapter, the entry point the Direct3D 9 runtime looks for.

diff -ru a/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/meson.build b/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/meson.build
--- a/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/meson.build
+++ b/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/meson.build
@@ -9,6 +9,14 @@
   'd3d10umd',
   files(
     'Adapter.cpp',
+    'D3D9Adapter.cpp',
+    'D3D9Common.cpp',
+    'D3D9Draw.cpp',
+    'D3D9Host.cpp',
+    'D3D9NineShader.c',
+    'D3D9Resource.cpp',
+    'D3D9ShaderTranslate.cpp',
+    'D3D9State.cpp',
     'Debug.cpp',
     'Device.cpp',
     'Draw.cpp',
diff -ru a/src/gallium/targets/d3d10umd/d3d10.def.in b/src/gallium/targets/d3d10umd/d3d10.def.in
--- a/src/gallium/targets/d3d10umd/d3d10.def.in
+++ b/src/gallium/targets/d3d10umd/d3d10.def.in
@@ -1,4 +1,5 @@
 ; stdcall calling convention have @number suffix on 32 bits architecture for gcc
+OpenAdapter@4
 OpenAdapter10@4
 OpenAdapter10_2@4
 D3DKMTAcquireKeyedMutex@4
